description:
crypto2dev_cipher() has two checks for authTagSz > CRYPTO2DEV_TAG_MAXLEN on the GCM encrypt path:

1. Early check (before pool acquire, ~line 707): if (chk_tagSz > CRYPTO2DEV_TAG_MAXLEN) return BUFFER_E;
2. Late check (after write/FINALIZE/read, ~line 889): if (authTagSz > CRYPTO2DEV_TAG_MAXLEN) { ret = BUFFER_E; goto done; }

For the encrypt path chk_tagSz == info->cipher.aesgcm_enc.authTagSz == authTagSz. Any value > 16 is caught by the early check and never reaches line 889. The late check is dead code.

The late check was the original fix for wolfssl-yjw.3 (oversized tag causing unauthenticated ciphertext to appear in out_buf before BUFFER_E). The early check was then added to catch the same condition before pool acquisition. The late check's comment ('Silently skipping GET_TAG would return 0 with a stale authTag buffer') describes a danger that no longer exists. The late check and its comment should be removed per the no-dead-code rule. No security impact — the early check fully covers this condition.
